{
  "_id": "jp0EIKxC9Ug9f1fj",
  "name": "Light's Vengeance",
  "type": "weapon",
  "img": "icons/weapons/hammers/hammer-double-steel-embossed.webp",
  "folder": "k5SXmlVACc2CKVy0",
  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Arthas Menethil wielded this weapon as a paladin of the Order of the Silver Hand, before his corruption made him the Lich King. The enormous, heavy hammer has a silver head etched with runes of power and a haft wrapped in blue leather, and it carries the blessing of the Light. Arthas cast it aside when he took up Frostmourne.</p><p><strong>Magic Weapon.</strong> You gain a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this weapon, and it deals an extra 2d10 Radiant damage to Undead.</p><p><strong>Repel Undead.</strong> While holding the weapon, you can take the Magic action to make brilliant light burst around you in a 30-foot Emanation. Each Undead in it makes a DC 20 Wisdom saving throw. On a failure, a target takes 4d8 Radiant damage and has the Frightened and Incapacitated conditions for 1 minute; while Frightened this way, it must use its movement on each of its turns to move as far from you as it can. The effect ends early on a target that takes any damage.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> Though blessed by the Light and wielded by its champion, the weapon carries the stain of the Lich King's corruption. It has 2 minor beneficial properties, 1 major beneficial property, and 2 minor detrimental properties (see <em>Artifact Traits</em> in the module journal).</p><p><strong>Destroying the Weapon.</strong> Striking Light's Vengeance with Frostmourne destroys the maul.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-4LSNGE9hK2ZtayfH\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Repel Undead affects only Undead: deselect the other targets.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
